{%- comment -%}
  The cart-level delivery warning — one wording, in one place.

  Two carts show it and they have to say the same thing. The /cart page renders this
  snippet directly (main-cart.liquid). The cart drawer is built client-side from /cart.js
  and cannot call a snippet, so theme.js renders these same strings out of
  window.ABM_SHIP.alerts, which snippets/shipping-config.liquid fills by rendering this
  snippet once per case. Before this the drawer carried its own shorter copy and the two
  drifted — a hood-plus-transmission cart reached checkout in the drawer with no
  split-order warning at all.

  kind (required): 'mixed' | 'pickup' | 'freight'
    mixed   — the cart holds a pickup-only part AND a part we ship; checkout can't take both
    pickup  — every line is pickup-only
    freight — the cart holds an LTL freight part (shown once 'mixed' is ruled out)

  The delivery group of a line comes from 'shipping-class', asked through 'shipping-group'
  style 'carrier'. This snippet names no tag and no rate, so it stays clear of
  scripts/check_contracts.py.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign phone_href = settings.phone | remove: '-' | remove: ' ' -%}
{%- case kind -%}

  {%- when 'mixed' -%}
    <div class="cart-alert">
      {% render 'icon', name: 'truck' %}
      <div>
        <b>Your cart mixes a pickup-only part with parts we ship.</b>
        <p>
          Checkout can't combine the two &mdash; body panels and glass are pickup or local
          delivery only, and the rest of your cart ships. Please place them as two separate
          orders, or call the yard and we'll do it for you in one go.
        </p>
        <p>
          {%- if settings.phone != blank -%}
            <a class="link" href="tel:{{ phone_href }}">{{ settings.phone }}</a> &middot;
          {%- endif -%}
          <a class="link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/freight">how pickup and freight work</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  {%- when 'pickup' -%}
    <div class="cart-alert">
      {% render 'icon', name: 'pin' %}
      <div>
        <b>Pickup only &mdash; Amite, Louisiana</b>
        <p>Choose <b>Pickup</b> at checkout. We'll have it at the counter within one business day, Monday&ndash;Friday 8&ndash;5.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  {%- when 'freight' -%}
    <div class="cart-alert">
      {% render 'icon', name: 'truck' %}
      <div>
        <b>Freight order &mdash; commercial address required</b>
        <p>
          One or more parts in your cart ship by LTL freight. They have to go to a business
          address with a forklift, or you can pick up at the freight terminal nearest you.
          We'll call to sort out delivery before anything ships.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/freight">how freight works</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

{%- endcase -%}
